# tests/lookaround/lookbehind_group_alt.rxt -- K123 (lane langfix2): a
# lookbehind ALTERNATIVE that is itself a non-capturing or scoped group with
# two or more alternatives. Such a group parses to a bare A_ALT, the same kind
# as the lookbehind's own top-level spine, and before the fix both the width
# rule and `vm_look_behind` read it AS spine and failed every such pattern
# with "internal error: a lookbehind body's alternation spine is longer than
# its reported branch count". The branch count the parse reported is now
# authoritative (`pcrec_lookbehind_branches`).
#
# Two halves. ACCEPTED: the group's alternatives share one length, so the
# top-level branch is fixed-width and compiles (first branch, later branch,
# scoped `(?i:...)`, the `(*plb:` spelling, negative, captures inside). And
# VARIABLE: the group's alternatives differ in length, libpcre2 10.46 accepts
# (variable-length lookbehind) and pcrec refuses by capability (§7.4, shape
# 5) -- a clean `perr`, the same answer `(?<=(a|bc))x` has always had, never
# the internal error.
#
# EVERY EXPECTATION WAS PRODUCED BY libpcre2 10.46 (tests/lib/p2gen.py over
# p2probe); the `perr` blocks are pcrec's documented capability refusal and
# libpcre2 ACCEPTS them, which each block's comment says.

# THE ADVERSARY'S CELL: a non-capturing group of two same-length alternatives.
pattern (?<=(?:ab|cd))x
features lookaround
m "cdx" 2 3
m "abx" 2 3
n "adx"
n "x"

# Three alternatives, one length.
pattern (?<=(?:ab|cd|ef))x
features lookaround
m "efx" 2 3
m "abx" 2 3
n "aex"

# The group is the FIRST of two top-level branches (it is what the spine walk
# leaves over), different length from the second.
pattern (?<=(?:ab|cd)|e)x
features lookaround
m "cdx" 2 3
m "ex" 1 2
n "dx"

# The group is the LAST top-level branch.
pattern (?<=e|(?:ab|cd))x
features lookaround
m "cdx" 2 3
m "ex" 1 2
n "bx"

# Captures inside the group: which alternative committed is observable.
pattern (?<=(?:(a)|(b)))x
features lookaround
m "bx" 1 2
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 0 1
m "ax" 1 2
g 1 0 1
g 2 -1 -1
n "cx"

# A scoped `(?i:...)` group (the adversary's second shape), same length.
pattern (?<=(?i:ab|cd))x
features lookaround,modifiers
m "CDx" 2 3
m "aBx" 2 3
n "cbx"

# The `(*plb:` spelling.
pattern (*plb:(?:ab|cd))x
features lookaround
m "abx" 2 3
n "acx"

# Negative polarity.
pattern (?<!(?:ab|cd))x
features lookaround
n "abx"
m "acx" 2 3
m "x" 0 1

# A counted repeat inside the group, same length.
pattern (?<=(?:a{2}|bc))x
features lookaround
m "aax" 2 3
m "bcx" 2 3
n "ax"

# Nested groups of alternatives.
pattern (?<=(?:a(?:b|c)|d(?:e|f)))x
features lookaround
m "acx" 2 3
m "dfx" 2 3
n "adx"

# VARIABLE: libpcre2 10.46 ACCEPTS (variable-length lookbehind); pcrec refuses by
# capability (§7.4), not by internal error.
pattern (?<=(?:a|bc))x
features lookaround
perr

# VARIABLE, scoped: libpcre2 10.46 ACCEPTS; pcrec refuses by capability.
pattern (?<=(?i:a|bc))x
features lookaround,modifiers
perr

# VARIABLE, the group first of two branches: libpcre2 10.46 ACCEPTS; pcrec
# refuses by capability.
pattern (?<=(?:a|bc)|d)x
features lookaround
perr

# VARIABLE, negative `(*plb:`-free spelling: libpcre2 10.46 ACCEPTS; pcrec
# refuses by capability.
pattern (?<!(?:a|bc))x
features lookaround
perr

